{0 Maildir for OCaml and Eio}

{!modules: Maildir}

The [maildir] package stores messages in the Dovecot Maildir layout, so
Dovecot and other Maildir programs can share a directory with it. Its
module is {!Maildir}, with {!Maildir.Keywords} for the keyword map and
{!Maildir.Dotlock} for scoped dotlocks.

{1 Format limits}

A message is one file in [new] or [cur]. Its flags live in the letters
after [:2,] in its filename. The system flags are [D] for Draft, [F] for
Flagged, [R] for Answered, [S] for Seen and [T] for Deleted. [P], for
Passed, has no IMAP flag and is kept across flag changes. The IMAP
Recent flag and unknown system flags cannot be stored and are
[Unsupported_flag].

A keyword takes one of the 26 lowercase letters [a] to [z]. The
[dovecot-keywords] file maps each letter to its keyword by index 0 to
25. A mapping, once written, is never reassigned. A keyword with no free
letter is [Too_many_keywords]. A filename letter that is neither a
system letter nor a mapped keyword fails the scan with [Unknown_letter].

A message's modification time is its date. {!Maildir.append} sets and
verifies [mtime] before it publishes the file, and a time that is not
finite or that the filesystem cannot store exactly is
[Unrepresentable_date]. {!Maildir.set_flags} renames the file and keeps
its basename, times, Passed letter and extra filename fields.

A nonempty legacy [.imap-flags] or [.imap-dates] directory is
[Legacy_metadata]. It needs offline migration and is never removed.

{1 Locks}

Scans, keyword map updates and mutations take the Dovecot metadata lock
[dovecot-uidlist.lock]. An existing lock raises
{!Maildir.Metadata_lock_busy} at once, including a stale one. No stale
lock is reclaimed automatically, since a pathname check and unlink can
remove another writer's fresh lock. Remove a stale lock offline, with
every user of the Maildir stopped.

{1 The writer}

Every mutation takes a {!Maildir.writer}. {!Maildir.with_writer} grants
one under an exclusive application lease on [.imap-writer.lock], which
serializes whole sync cycles. A second lease on the same Maildir, from
this process or another, raises {!Maildir.Writer_lock_busy}, and a writer
used after its callback returns raises {!Maildir.Writer_expired}. Do not
remove the lease file or fork while holding it. Dovecot and other
external programs do not take the lease, and they must honour the
metadata lock for a complete scan to prove a message absent.

Format and policy failures are {!Maildir.error} results. I/O failures
raise [Eio.Io], and the exceptions above report concurrency.

{1 Example}

The program below creates a Maildir, delivers one message with the Seen
flag, a keyword and a fixed date, adds the Flagged flag, and counts the
messages. It is [test/examples/writer.ml], which the build compiles and
never runs. {!Maildir.open_dir} creates [new], [cur] and [tmp] but not
the Maildir itself.

{[
let ( let* ) = Result.bind

let important =
  match Mail_flag.Imap_flag.keyword "$Important" with
  | Ok keyword -> keyword
  | Error message -> invalid_arg message

let deliver maildir message =
  Maildir.with_writer maildir @@ fun writer ->
  let* occurrence =
    Maildir.append writer ~source:(Eio.Flow.string_source message)
      ~length:(Int64.of_int (String.length message))
      ~flags:[ Mail_flag.Imap_flag.system Seen; important ]
      ~mtime:1_700_000_000. ()
  in
  Maildir.set_flags writer occurrence
    (Mail_flag.Imap_flag.system Flagged :: occurrence.flags)

let () =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  let path = Eio.Path.(Eio.Stdenv.fs env / "Mail" / "INBOX") in
  Eio.Path.mkdirs ~exists_ok:true ~perm:0o700 path;
  let result =
    let* maildir = Maildir.open_dir path in
    let* occurrence = deliver maildir "Subject: hello\r\n\r\nHello.\r\n" in
    print_endline occurrence.filename;
    Maildir.fold maildir ~init:0 ~f:(fun n _ -> n + 1)
  in
  match result with
  | Ok count -> Printf.printf "%d messages\n" count
  | Error e ->
      Format.eprintf "maildir: %a@." Maildir.pp_error e;
      exit 1
]}
